Third-party components
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

JavaMP3 (fr.delthas:javamp3), https://github.com/delthas/JavaMP3
  MIT License. Pure-Java MP3 decoder used by the lyrics module, bundled inside the Fabric jars.

Fonts of the lyrics module (src/main/resources/assets/vibeyclient/font/lyrics/, Fabric jars only):
  Bebas Neue, Kaushan Script (brush), Bungee, Caveat, Fredoka, Kanit, Monoton, Montserrat, Pacifico, Poppins,
  Press Start 2P and Unbounded under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; Permanent Marker (marker) under the
  Apache License 2.0. License texts: licenses/lyrics/fonts/ (inside every Fabric jar under
  licenses/vibeyclient/lyrics/).

Optional components of the video screens (Fabric 1.21.11) – NOT included in the jars. They are downloaded only
after the user agrees in an in-game prompt that names size, source and licence (docs/VIDEO.md):
  FFmpeg (LGPL-2.1-or-later "lgpl-shared" Windows build from https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds), run as a
    separate program, unpacked to <game dir>/vibeyclient/ffmpeg/ together with its LICENSE.txt. An FFmpeg already
    installed on the system is used as is.
  MCEF Modern (https://github.com/DimasKama/mcef-modern, LGPL-2.1), installed unmodified into mods/ from Modrinth;
    it downloads JCEF/CEF/Chromium (BSD-3-Clause and the Chromium third-party licences) from Maven Central
    (me.friwi:jcef-natives-*). The client only compiles against its API.
  YouTube videos are shown only through YouTube's official embedded player; the YouTube Terms of Service apply.

